# Sorting Algorithm readme
 These are the must known sorting algorithms:
 1. Selection sort
 2. Bubble sort
 3. Insertion sort
 4. Merge sort
 5. Quick sort
 6. Heap sort


## Problems (easy to hard)

Work top to bottom. Each level adds one new idea on top of the last.

### Level 1 - Implement the algorithms yourself
Idea: write selection, bubble, insertion, merge, quick and heap sort on this one problem.

LeetCode 912.     Sort an Array                                   -- write each sort here, compare timings
LeetCode 88.      Merge Sorted Array                              -- the merge step, from the back

### Level 2 - Use sorting to simplify the problem
Idea: sort first, then the answer becomes a scan.

LeetCode 75.      Sort Colors                                     -- counting / Dutch flag - DONE
LeetCode 1122.    Relative Sort Array
LeetCode 56.      Merge Intervals
LeetCode 179.     Largest Number                                  -- custom comparator
LeetCode 451.     Sort Characters By Frequency

### Level 3 - Sorting variants
Idea: bucket / counting sort and quickselect.

LeetCode 347.     Top K Frequent Elements                         -- bucket sort by frequency
LeetCode 215.     Kth Largest Element in an Array                 -- quickselect, O(n) average
LeetCode 148.     Sort List                                       -- merge sort on a linked list

### Level 4 - Hard (merge sort as a counting tool)
Idea: count pairs while merging two sorted halves.

LeetCode 315.     Count of Smaller Numbers After Self
LeetCode 493.     Reverse Pairs
